# Project: Halden Licence Translation

Temporary product name: Halden Licence Translation. Replace it later in lib/copy.ts.

## What the product is
A private service that produces a multilingual translation of a customer's valid
domestic driving licence (digital PDF + optional printed card). It is NOT an
International Driving Permit, is NOT government-issued, and does NOT grant
driving rights.

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind
- Prisma + PostgreSQL
- Stripe Checkout for payments
- Resend for email
- Cloudflare R2 (S3 API) for uploaded files and generated PDFs
- @react-pdf/renderer for PDF generation
- Zod for validation

## HARD COPY RULES (never violate, in any file, including metadata)
- Never use the words "permit", "IDP", "IDD" or "International Driving
  Permit" to describe our product. Only mention them when explaining what
  the official document is and where to get it.
- Never claim "valid in X countries", "accepted worldwide", "drive legally",
  "avoid fines", "trusted by police", or that any rental company accepts it.
- Never show third-party company logos.
- Never invent reviews, customer counts or ratings.
- Show this notice only in the site footer, not above buy buttons:
  "This is a translation of your existing driving licence. It is not an
  International Driving Permit, is not issued by any government, and does not
  give you the right to drive. Check your destination's requirements."
- Describe the product as: "multilingual translation of your valid licence
  to help others read your details abroad."

## Code rules
- Server-side validation with Zod on every API route
- Never trust client prices; compute amounts server-side
- Store files privately; serve via signed URLs
- Env vars in .env.example, never hardcode secrets
- Small components, no giant files; add loading and error states
